# Ablo Marketing OS — learning ledger (append-only, git-tracked).
# The marketing-os-refresh agent reads this FIRST every run and writes to it LAST.
# This is how the OS compounds judgment over time: predict -> observe -> score -> distill.
#
# Two record types, one JSON object per line:
#
#  prediction  a falsifiable bet logged when you ship a fix or conclude an experiment.
#    {"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-YYYY-MM-DD-slug","date":"YYYY-MM-DD","action":"...",
#     "linked":"OS-... | PH-#### | CC-rank-N","metric":"<history.jsonl key>","baseline":N,
#     "predicted":N,"horizon_days":N,"due":"YYYY-MM-DD","rationale":"...","status":"open"}
#   when its horizon elapses, resolve it in place:
#     ...,"status":"resolved","actual":N,"verdict":"hit|partial|miss","resolved_date":"YYYY-MM-DD","lesson_id":"LES-..."
#
#  lesson  a durable heuristic distilled from a resolved bet or the weekly audit.
#    {"type":"lesson","id":"LES-YYYY-MM-DD-slug","date":"YYYY-MM-DD","lesson":"...",
#     "evidence":"...","confidence":"high|med|low","tags":["funnel","paid",...],"source_pred":"PRED-..."}
#
# Rules: never rewrite history except to resolve an open prediction. Keep lessons to one
# sentence, lead with the result, cite evidence. metric must be a real history.jsonl key.
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-05-20-google-signup","date":"2026-05-20","action":"Make Google the primary signup option (OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE)","linked":"OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE","metric":"signup_completion_rate","baseline":33,"predicted":42,"horizon_days":10,"due":"2026-05-30","rationale":"Google one-tap removes password friction at the highest-drop step.","status":"resolved","actual":44,"verdict":"hit","resolved_date":"2026-05-31","lesson_id":"LES-2026-05-31-friction","note":"Beat the call: predicted +9pp, landed +11pp."}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-05-31-friction","date":"2026-05-31","lesson":"Removing auth friction at the signup step is the highest-ROI funnel move so far: Google-primary lifted completion 33% to 44% (+11pp).","evidence":"OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE before/after; PRED-2026-05-20-google-signup resolved hit.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","signup","friction"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-05-20-google-signup"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-03-cpl","date":"2026-06-03","lesson":"The current signup-launch flight runs CPL ~$7.79, roughly 3x cheaper than the prior flight's $21.04. Keep budget on the current creative+targeting before testing new angles.","evidence":"history.jsonl 2026-06-03 cpl=7.79 vs prior-flight lifetime CPL $21.04 (.refresh.log 2026-06-02).","confidence":"med","tags":["paid","meta","cpl"]}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-03-activate-flow","date":"2026-06-03","action":"Wire the Activate A1-A3 Klaviyo flow (re-engage signups with no model generated in 24h) to lift activation","linked":"CC-rank-2","metric":"activation_rate","baseline":69,"predicted":75,"horizon_days":21,"due":"2026-06-24","rationale":"31% of signups never generate a first model; an automated 24h nudge built from existing templates should recover a meaningful share. Modest call: calibration is thin (n=1) and traffic is low. Conditional on the flow going live; if unshipped by due date, mark moot.","status":"resolved","actual":50,"verdict":"miss","resolved_date":"2026-06-24","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-24-activate-miss"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link","date":"2026-06-04","action":"Remove magic-link from signup modal entirely, leaving Google as the sole in-modal auth path","linked":"CC-rank-4","metric":"signup_completion_rate","baseline":42,"predicted":50,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-06-18","rationale":"Email clicks (64) still out-pace Google (59) despite Google being primary since May 27; magic-link completion is 7% (4 of 58 requesters log in). Demotion is not enough. Removing the option eliminates the dominant failure path at the source. Prior Google-primary lift was +11pp from a similar modal simplification, so another 8pp from removal is plausible.","status":"resolved","actual":46,"verdict":"miss","resolved_date":"2026-06-18","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-18-modal-ceiling"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-04-homepage-cro","date":"2026-06-04","action":"Homepage + paid-landing CRO: sharper hero from the bodies-you-cannot-shoot wedge (mkt1-homepage-positioning lens), rebuild /toddler to match /plus-size, UTM-tag variants","linked":"CC-rank-5","metric":"home_signup_pct","baseline":6.7,"predicted":8.0,"horizon_days":45,"due":"2026-07-19","rationale":"Homepage is ~63% of entry volume (540 of 855) at 6.7% signup; biggest leak by raw volume (78% sitewide bounce, land->engage 22%). Live proof the page is the lever, not the ad: /toddler 2.2% vs /plus-size 6.8% signup, and paid Swim converts 4% on the landing despite the best CPL ($2.22). A sharper hero should lift homepage signup. SCORING: resolve on the hero_v2 UTM cohort signup rate vs hero_v1 (post-ship, >=2 weeks of traffic), NOT the blended 60d home_signup_pct, which dilutes a mid-window ship; home_signup_pct is the directional indicator only. Conditional: needs Product to ship the variant (escalated, user-visible). If unshipped by due, mark MOOT (not miss). Calibration thin (n=1) so a modest +1.3pp call.","status":"open","scoring":"hero_v2 vs hero_v1 UTM-cohort signup rate, post-ship >=14d; home_signup_pct directional only; moot if unshipped by due"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-qa-figures","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"Derive headline visitor/land counts from the build's own data.js at write time, never hand-carry a number across a session: an off-by-3 (537 vs live 540) crept in because the figure was retyped from an earlier read while the 60d window moved.","evidence":"QA numbers lens caught 537/854 in content.json+ledger vs live data.js 540/855.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process","numbers"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-qa-rolling-metric","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"A rolling N-day aggregate cannot cleanly score a fix that ships mid-window; bind the prediction to a post-ship or UTM-isolated cohort window or it scores 'miss' for dilution, not truth.","evidence":"QA calls lens: home_signup_pct is a 60d-trailing aggregate (build.py LANDING_Q INTERVAL 60 DAY); PRED-2026-06-04-homepage-cro re-plumbed to score on the hero_v2 UTM cohort.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","measurement"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-qa-roadmap-winprob","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"On a roadmap ranked by leverage x win-probability, a test blocked on another team has near-zero NEAR-TERM win-prob; rank launchable-today tests first and label the blocked one's win-prob 'low (blocked)', even if its leverage is highest.","evidence":"QA calls lens: hero-rebuild CRO was ranked roadmap #1 but needs Product to build the variant; re-ordered below the buildable-today Activate flow.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","roadmap","prioritization"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-try-landing","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"[SUPERSEDED by LES-2026-06-04-try-mismeasure: the 1.5% was an attribution artifact; true /try view->signup ~4.4%.] The /try value-first paid landing badly underperforms the homepage for signups: 1.5% (1/68 visitors) vs 7.4% (42/568); route paid to the homepage and do not fund /try further until it is fixed or the test is powered.","evidence":"data.js landingPages 2026-06-04: / = 42/568 (7.4%), /try = 1/68 (1.5%), /try-kids = 0/13; OS-TRY-VS-HOME running, /try arm thin (1 conversion).","confidence":"med","tags":["funnel","paid","cro","try"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-try-mismeasure","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"The /try landing 'signup %' in landingPages is an attribution artifact, not the real rate: keying signup_completed to first-pageview pathname=/try caught only 2 of 24 actual signup-wall reaches and credited 3 of 4 /try-flow signups to other pages. Measure /try by its own tbs_* funnel: 91 viewed -> 25 generate -> 24 wall -> 4 signed = 4.4% view->signup (16.7% wall->signup). Signup tracking itself is fine (the wall->modal->signup chain fires); the landing-page attribution is what is broken.","evidence":"HogQL 30d: entry=/try=68/12/2/2/1 vs tbs_ taxonomy=91 page_viewed/54 category/25 generate/24 wall/4 signed; the 4 tbs signups attribute to entry=/ (2), /try (1), /onboarding (1).","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","tracking","measurement","funnel","try"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-04-anon-funnel-reach","date":"2026-06-04","lesson":"When measuring an anonymous flow's funnel (e.g. /try tbs_*), count each step's OWN distinct-user reach; do not intersect deeper steps on the entry event's person-set. PostHog re-splits anonymous person_ids across steps, so the intersection silently drops most users (the cohort query read generate=5 vs the true reach of 25). Endpoints (page-view, signup) are the reliable anchors; a multi-event union step over-counts and is best dropped.","evidence":"build.py _correct_try_row: intersected-on-tbs_page_viewed gave [91,17,5,5,4]; per-event reach gave [91,118,25,24,4]; shipped funnel uses the monotonic spine 91 land -> 25 generate -> 24 wall -> 4 signup = 4.4%.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","tracking","measurement","funnel","engineering"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-05-post-aha-email","date":"2026-06-05","action":"Wire post-AHA conversion email flow in Klaviyo (trigger: Try-on Completed, no Checkout Started in 48h) to lift checkout starts","linked":"CC-rank-4","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":8,"predicted":12,"horizon_days":21,"due":"2026-06-26","rationale":"39 users have reached the aha try-on; only 7 started checkout (18%). The other 32 (82%) received no nudge at peak intent. A single behavioral email at the aha moment with a pricing CTA should recover a meaningful share. Conservative: +4pp lift on thin base. Conditional on the flow going live; if unshipped by due date, mark moot.","scoring":"Resolve on the checkout_started count among post-flow-live aha-reachers vs the pre-flow baseline (7/39=18%). payment_rate (checkout_started/total_signups) is the directional indicator but dilutes as signups grow; only use it if denominator growth is <20% over the window.","status":"resolved","resolved_date":"2026-06-29","actual":5,"verdict":"miss","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-29-post-aha-email-miss"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-05-qa-modal-peak","date":"2026-06-05","lesson":"Modal completion peaks in the first 10-day window post-ship then normalizes to a lower steady state: the Google-primary lift scored +11pp (33→44%) at day 10 but the all-window rate settled at +4pp (33→37%). Score conversion-fix predictions at 30-day steady state, not the peak window.","evidence":"PRED-2026-05-20-google-signup resolved hit at 44% (10-day window); data.js 2026-06-05 OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE after=37.2% (55/148 all post-May-27). QA catch: the CC rank-9 done item claimed '42%, held' but the live experiments signal shows 37%.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","signup","measurement","predictions"]}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-09-tbs-category-fix","date":"2026-06-09","action":"Simplify the /try category-selection UI to reduce the 60% pre-category bounce (larger tap targets, one-line descriptor per category, or pre-selected default)","linked":"CC-rank-3","metric":"home_signup_pct","baseline":10.5,"predicted":13.0,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-06-23","rationale":"251 people viewed /try since Jun 4, only 101 selected a category (40%); after that the funnel holds well (57% wall to signup). The loss is entirely at step one. /try is now the default paid landing (OS-TRY-VS-HOME concluded Jun 8). A 15pp category-selection lift converts roughly 9 more signups per 251 visitors at current downstream rates. Modest call: thin sample (5 days of data), no prior similar fix to calibrate against. SCORING: resolve on post-fix /try cohort view to signup rate vs Jun 9 baseline (27/256 = 10.5%). Uses home_signup_pct as the nearest landing-page signup rate key; scoring note is the binding measurement spec. Moot if the UI fix is not shipped by due date.","status":"resolved","scoring":"post-fix /try cohort view->signup rate vs 10.5% baseline (27/256); >=14d tbs* data required; moot if unshipped by due date","actual":10.4,"verdict":"moot","resolved_date":"2026-06-24","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-24-tbs-category-miss","resolution_note":"moot: gating action never shipped/executed (per the prediction own moot-if-unshipped clause); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-09-qa-metric-key","date":"2026-06-09","lesson":"signup_completion_rate is reserved for modal-open to signup (modal completion %, range 33-50); landing-page view-to-signup rates belong under home_signup_pct or a page-specific key like try_signup_pct. Mixing them makes predictions unscorable without reading the scoring note.","evidence":"QA check on PRED-2026-06-09-tbs-category-fix: baseline 10.5 is the /try view->signup rate, not a modal rate; prior predictions using signup_completion_rate had baselines of 33-42 (modal completion range). Revised metric to home_signup_pct as the nearest correct key.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","measurement"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-try-value-first","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Routing paid to value-first /try pages is a defensible default but NOT a measured win: /try 9.9% (28/282, tbs cohort) vs home 8.8% (59/668, first-pageview method) is statistical noise, /try-kids 8.6% vs /toddler 3.9% is under-powered, and the arms use different attribution methods. No evidence value-first is worse; default to it and spend testing energy down-funnel.","evidence":"data.js 2026-06-10 landingPages (live figures); OS-TRY-VS-HOME retired 2026-06-08; LES-2026-06-04-try-mismeasure documents the attribution asymmetry contaminating the control.","confidence":"low","tags":["paid","cro","landing"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-ab-power-floor","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Product-surface A/Bs cannot reach power at current traffic: coachmarks PH-374260 collected 73 exposures (32/41) in 11 days vs the ~200/variant floor; at this traffic prefer ship-and-measure before/after (OS-...) over a PostHog split.","evidence":"PH-374260 ended in PostHog 2026-06-09, inconclusive; exposures from a live HogQL read 2026-06-10 (not yet persisted in data.js, treat as unaudited).","confidence":"med","tags":["experiments","process","power"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-attribution-method","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Never log a landing winner whose arms use different attribution methods: /try (tbs_* cohort) vs home (first-pageview pathname, known to mis-credit value-first signups to /) is not a comparison; re-derive both arms under one method before any beats/loses lesson.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-10 caught LES try-value-first drafted at med on mismatched arms; downgraded to low and reframed.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","measurement","cro"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-denominator-splice","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Name numerator event, denominator cohort, and window for every rate written into the OS: today spliced a spine numerator onto an aha denominator (9/54; real: 11 lifetime pricing reach, 9/125 spine) and quoted lifetime tryon-rate cohorts (Meta 32% vs Direct 57%) as last-7d model-rate evidence.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-10, refutations on CC ranks 3-4.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","numbers"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-pred-metric-compliance","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Citing a QA lesson in a prediction rationale while keeping the metric it forbids is acknowledgment-without-compliance: reject any prediction bound to a flight-cumulative or rolling aggregate when the action shipped mid-window; hold the bet until a clean cohort metric exists.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-10 refuted PRED-try-paid-default (flight-cumulative cpl, autopilot confound, rollout premise overstated); prediction held, not logged.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-run-provenance","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Persist what you act on and what you cite: empty run logs made the coachmarks 100%-flag and the paid-default rollout unauditable, and live-read ad-set figures (imps/PV, 24h CPL) were unverifiable; record executed actions in run-*.json and either persist live-read figures or do not cite them.","evidence":"QA boundary lens 2026-06-10: run-2026-06-08/10.json effectively empty; $24.42 not derivable (history gives $23.64); /toddler 800/10/0 in no persisted source.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout","date":"2026-06-10","action":"Run price-ask test: manually onboard 5 Kids and 5 Swim founders this week, walk each to try-on, ask for card; combined with Convert C4 paid-ask emails reaching first-wave aha users around Jun 13","linked":"CC-rank-1","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":10,"predicted":13,"horizon_days":15,"due":"2026-06-25","rationale":"Two parallel mechanisms: (1) 10 founders hand-walked to try-on, conservative 30% checkout rate = 3 new starters; (2) Convert C4 fires for aha users in the flow since Jun 6, adding further intent. Combined: 10 to 13. Distinct from PRED-2026-06-05-post-aha-email (baseline 8, email-only, current count already at 10). Moot if price-ask test not started by Jun 17.","scoring":"checkout_started reach >= 13 by Jun 25; moot if price-ask test not started by Jun 17","status":"resolved","actual":6,"verdict":"miss","resolved_date":"2026-06-17","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-17-price-ask-moot"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-10-qa-live-vs-curated-funnel","date":"2026-06-10","lesson":"Always read data.js .live.funnel (live HogQL, updated daily) not .funnelCurated (cached snapshot, updated Jun 3): the cached section showed 64 signups/30 tryons/8 checkouts while the live section showed 125/54/10; nearly overwrote correct commandCenter status text with wrong numbers.","evidence":"QA catch Jun 10: live.funnel.stages checkout all=10, tryon all=54, signup all=125 vs funnelCurated 8/30/64. The commandCenter items correctly use live figures. Edits to rank-2 and rank-3 were held after QA.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process","numbers"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-kids-pixel-swap","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"A creative swap to a new landing URL requires pixel verification before routing paid traffic: the Jun-8 /toddler→/try-kids swap produced an unaudited signal of 0 PageViews on 12 clicks, potentially $16/day burning blind on the top-spend segment.","evidence":"Campaigns read-agent live-read 2026-06-11 (unaudited -- not in history.jsonl or data.js); autopilot TRACKING_ISSUE flag on Kids adset.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","paid","meta","pixel","tracking"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-adsegment-unpersisted","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"Never cite ad-set-level figures (segment CPL, per-adset PageViews, impression counts) as facts unless they appear verbatim in data.js or history.jsonl. data.js explicitly warns these are not persisted; live-read figures must be written to a persisted record before they can be cited in decisions.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-11: Swim CPL $0.51 absent from all sources (nearest $2.22); Kids 0-PageViews claim sourced from live read only; data.js commandCenter rank 5 body explicitly states 'ad-set-level counts are not persisted'.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","paid","meta","numbers"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-exp-snapshot-vs-live","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The OS-SIGNUP-GOOGLE 'after' field in data.js (44.7%, 105/235) is a frozen May-27 cohort snapshot, not the current signup_completion_rate. Use live.funnel intent→signup d7 for current scoring (52.8% as of Jun 11).","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-11: d7 modal intent=106, signup=56 → 52.8%, exceeds the 50% prediction target. 44.7% is a stale cohort field.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","signup","measurement","predictions"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-funnel-rank","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"Under a first-paying-customer goal, upstream funnel gates (activation) must rank above downstream optimizations (/try UX, pixel attribution) that can only affect users who already passed the upstream gate.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-11: 43% activation (54% rolling) means 57% of signups never reach the paywall; ranking category-fix above activation gap is structurally backwards.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","prioritization"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-qa-pred-early-flag","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"When a prediction's current value is below the pre-intervention baseline (not just below the target), flag it as a directional miss immediately regardless of the due date -- the trajectory itself is informative under short goal timelines.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-11: PRED-2026-06-03-activate-flow target 75, baseline 69, current 54 -- below baseline, not just below target. 13 days to due, 19 days to end-June goal.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","process"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-kids-pixel-not-a-bug","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The Kids '/try-kids 0 PageViews' alarm is a Meta-side reporting artifact (ad-block asymmetry), NOT a code bug: PostHog independently recorded 122 paid pageviews / 101 people on /try-kids in 14d. SPA rewrite + base pixel + no consent gate all verified correct. Reverting to /toddler would not help (identical architecture). Real fix is server-side Meta CAPI, a Jason build.","evidence":"PostHog $pageview on /try-kids: 135/106 (14d), 122 utm_source=meta; vercel.json /(.*)→index.html; index.html:31-32 base pixel.","confidence":"high","tags":["paid","meta","pixel","tracking","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-activation-mixshift-confirmed","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"The activation decline is CONFIRMED mix-shift, not a product regression: paid activates 44% vs direct 66% (30d, signup→model_generated), and paid's share of signups rose from 50% (30d) to 73% (7d), dragging the blend down. Direct still activates 48-66% so the product step is intact. Fix is traffic quality + the live Activate flow, not emergency product work.","evidence":"PostHog activation-by-channel 2026-06-11: meta/paid 44.0%(50) vs direct 66.0%(47) 30d; paid share 50→73% across 30d→7d windows.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","activation","paid","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-11-purchase-wiring-ok","date":"2026-06-11","lesson":"purchase_completed wiring is correct end-to-end (Stripe success_url=/account?success=true → AccountPage fires track, keyed to user.id matching the funnel person). 0 fires ≈ 0 real completed purchases (10 started, 0 paid), not a tracking bug; confirm in Stripe. Robustness gap: client-side fire is ad-blockable; bulletproof fix is server-side capture from the existing checkout.session.completed webhook (no server PostHog client yet, so a Jason build).","evidence":"stripe.routes.ts:74, stripe.service.ts:109/139, AccountPage.tsx:44-52, analytics.ts:27; no posthog-node in apps/server.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","payment","tracking","diagnosis"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Meta ads went dark: $0 spend + 0 impressions across all 4 segments for 3+ days (Jun 13-15), and the dashboard's $8.33 CPL is a frozen lifetime average (241.52/29), not a live read. A 'Live' status with a flat CPL can mask zero delivery — always check incremental spend, not the CPL tile.","evidence":"history.jsonl spend_lifetime frozen 241.52 Jun13-15, cpl 8.33 + signups_meta 29 identical; autopilot plan_actions=[] '0 impressions' every cycle.","confidence":"high","tags":["paid","meta","delivery","ops"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-metric-mislabel","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Only cite an X%→Y% before/after when both numbers label the SAME metric: a draft claimed the Jun-12 overhaul moved signup→model 41→43, but 41 is the signup→activation goal tile and 43 is the open→signup modal leak, neither is signup→model (67% reach). Grep the exact values and confirm the metric before asserting a movement.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-15: 41% and 43% tag different data.js tiles; daily models/signups ratio too noisy to source a clean before/after.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","numbers","measurement"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-window-zero","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"A '0 in the last N days' claim must be checked across the whole window, not the tail: 'payment_rate 10→6, 0 checkouts in 10 days' was wrong, the recent series is 7→6 (10 was the prediction baseline) and checkouts were 1 on Jun 8 and 1 on Jun 10, only Jun 13-15 were zero.","evidence":"QA numbers lens 2026-06-15: history.jsonl payment_rate Jun7-15=7,7,7,7,7,6,6,6,6; checkouts Jun8=1, Jun10=1.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","numbers"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-confound-vs-fail","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"Do not conflate 'confounded/unidentifiable' with 'failed': when channel mix-shift confounds activation, a shipped overhaul's effect is unmeasurable, not zero. Asserting both 'it's mix-shift' and 'the overhaul didn't move it' is incoherent, the honest call is 'effect unreadable, bind a clean before/after.'","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-15 on the activation-gap item; numbers lens confirmed no clean pre/post series exists.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","measurement","predictions"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-qa-source-pin","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"QA skeptics must verify against the run's actual sources (data.js + history.jsonl), not a same-named MCP graph: a skeptic this run read the 'marketingos' MCP (an unrelated hiring graph) and could not verify anything, voiding its data-dependent verdicts. Pin the file paths in the skeptic brief and tell it not to use MCP workspaces.","evidence":"QA calls lens 2026-06-15 returned 'workspace is CodeSignal hiring graph, n=0'; its logic points held but data claims were void.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","process"]}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-12-channel-quality-gap","date":"2026-06-12","lesson":"Direct/organic users convert to checkout at 13.4% (9/67 signups) vs Meta users at 1.4% (1/69 signups): a 10x downstream quality gap. 9 of 10 all-time checkouts came from the Direct channel. For the first paying customer, prioritize manual outreach to high-intent Direct/LinkedIn cohort (Wave 1/2 referrals) over cold Meta signups.","evidence":"live.channels.attribution Jun 12: Direct 596 users, 67 signups, 39 tryons, 9 checkouts; Meta 916 users, 69 signups, 21 tryons, 1 checkout. N=10 checkouts total, so treat as med confidence.","confidence":"med","tags":["funnel","paid","meta","channels","conversion"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-12-studio-rageclicks","date":"2026-06-12","action":"Escalate the /studio rage-click cluster to Jason as a concrete product UX bug report (33 users, 70 events, recurring daily: Jun 7=8, Jun 11=7) and ship the specific control fix","linked":"CC-rank-4","metric":"activation_rate","baseline":53,"predicted":58,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-06-26","rationale":"The /studio UX barrier is persistent and daily, independent of channel mix-shift: 24% of studio entrants rage-click. The mix-shift diagnosis (LES-2026-06-11-activation-mixshift-confirmed) explains the blended-rate decline but not the daily rage-click pattern. Fixing the blocked control should recover some non-activators. Conservative 5pp call: baseline 53% (75/141 spine signup→model_generated Jun 12). Moot if no product fix shipped by due date.","scoring":"spine model_generated/signup % post-fix vs Jun 12 baseline of 53% (75/141); require >=14d post-fix cohort data; moot if fix not shipped by due date","status":"resolved","resolved_date":"2026-06-29","actual":49,"verdict":"miss","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-29-rageclicks-miss"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark-RETRACTED","date":"2026-06-15","lesson":"RETRACTS LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark. Meta was NOT dark. The Meta API shows healthy daily spend Jun 8-14 ($17-58/day, ~$277/wk, 27k impressions Jun 14). The OS's Meta feed went STALE around Jun 12 (build.py carried $241.52/29 signups forward), and a frozen lifetime CPL ($8.33) was misread as $0 incremental spend. Lesson: verify a 'something stopped' alarm against the SOURCE (Meta API / Ads Manager) before raising it, a flat dashboard number is more often a broken feed than a real outage.","evidence":"ads_get_ad_entities account 3682177848625068 last_7d daily: Jun8 $57.96/2900imp ... Jun14 $41.68/26979imp; OS data.js spend frozen 241.52 since Jun 12.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","paid","meta","measurement","process"]}
{"type": "prediction", "id": "PRED-2026-06-16-aha-cta-rework", "date": "2026-06-16", "action": "Rewrite AHA flow B1 and B2 CTAs with a direct action link and concrete value line, replacing the zero-click current CTA (B1: 11 recipients, 36.4% open, 0 clicks; B2: 9 recipients, 33.3% open, 0 clicks)", "linked": "CC-rank-2", "metric": "payment_rate", "baseline": 6, "predicted": 8, "horizon_days": 14, "due": "2026-06-30", "rationale": "Both deployed AHA messages have strong opens (36.4% B1, 33.3% B2) and 0 clicks across 20 combined recipient-opens. Opens confirm deliverability and intent; 0 clicks is a copy or link failure. If 2-3 of 11 B1 readers click to /studio and 1-2 start checkout, payment_rate reaches 8% (12+ checkouts on 155+ signups). Window closing: users cycle out of the flow. Conservative call on thin sample (9 all-time checkouts). Conditional on rework shipping by Jun 21.", "scoring": "payment_rate >= 8 by 2026-06-30; spine denominator 155+; moot if B1/B2 CTAs not rewritten by 2026-06-21", "status": "resolved", "actual": 5, "verdict": "moot", "resolved_date": "2026-07-01", "lesson_id": "LES-2026-07-01-aha-cta-moot", "resolution_note": "moot: AHA CTA rework never shipped (B1/B2 still 0.0% click, email_click pinned 0 all window); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-16-qa-modal-d7-drift","date":"2026-06-16","lesson":"The d7 modal completion rate drifts as the 7-day window rolls: the Jun-15 CC rank-8 status cited 52.8% but today's live data shows 34/71 = 47.9%, which is below the PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link target of 50%. Never carry a prior d7 figure forward; recompute from live.funnel.stages d7 intent and signup counts each run.","evidence":"live.funnel.stages d7: intent=71, signup=34 -> 34/71=47.9%. Jun-15 CC rank-8 status cited 52.8% from a different d7 window cut.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","signup","measurement","predictions"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-17-price-ask-moot","date":"2026-06-17","lesson":"When a price-ask test has a moot condition ('moot if not started by date X') and that date arrives without the test running, resolve the prediction as a miss rather than leaving it open: the causal mechanism was never activated, but the outcome is still real and the ledger must close. The next action is not a fresh prediction of the same bet -- it is a narrower, more concrete outreach to the highest-intent contacts already in the funnel.","evidence":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout moot condition fired Jun 17: test not started despite being rank-1 for 7 days. payment_rate stayed at 6 (baseline stated in prediction was 10). Resolved miss.","confidence":"high","tags":["predictions","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-10-price-ask-checkout"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-17-checkout-outreach","date":"2026-06-17","action":"Personal 1:1 outreach to each of the 10 Direct-channel checkout starters before Jun 20; confirm their Stripe dropout reason, offer concierge onboarding, close the first purchase","linked":"CC-rank-1","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":6,"predicted":8,"horizon_days":7,"due":"2026-06-24","rationale":"10 people have started checkout (9 from Direct, 1 from Meta) and 0 have paid. These are the highest-intent contacts in the funnel: they saw pricing, clicked through to Stripe, and stopped. A personal email asking what got in the way is the surest path to the first paying customer. Direct converts to checkout at 14.1% (10/71 signups) vs Meta 1.2% (1/81 signups). Even 1 completion plus 2 more new checkouts = 13/159 = 8.2% payment_rate. Conditional: requires reaching at least 5 of the 10 checkout starters before Jun 20.","scoring":"payment_rate >= 8 OR paying_customers >= 1 by 2026-06-24; moot if no personal outreach to checkout starters before Jun 20","status":"resolved","actual":5,"verdict":"moot","resolved_date":"2026-06-24","lesson_id":"LES-2026-06-24-checkout-outreach-miss","resolution_note":"moot: gating action never shipped/executed (per the prediction own moot-if-unshipped clause); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-17-qa-c4-timing","date":"2026-06-17","lesson":"A 0% open rate on a triggered email may be a timing artifact rather than a deliverability failure when the recipient count is small and the send is recent: if the 7-day delay window elapsed within the last 24-48h, the emails may simply not have had time to be opened. Verify send timestamps against the trigger event date before treating 0% open as actionable. C1's 100% open is a different cohort (different trigger window) and cannot serve as a control.","evidence":"QA Jun 17: C4 Convert flow (Day 7 paid-ask) shows 0% open across 5 recipients. C1 same flow shows 100% open on 5 different recipients. Flagged as high-sev in CC rank 4 but conditioned on Klaviyo delivery log verification through Jun 20.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","lifecycle","email","measurement"],"source_pred":null}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-18-modal-ceiling","date":"2026-06-18","lesson":"Removing magic-link lifted modal completion from 33% to ~45% (all-time) but not to the 50% target: the ceiling appears to be in-modal OAuth friction (desktop lags mobile, consent screen adds a step), not the inbox round-trip that was the baseline culprit. The next modal fix requires reducing in-modal friction, not removing more options.","evidence":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link resolved miss Jun 18: d7 completion 28/61=45.9%, all-time post-May-27 132/293=45.1%, both below 50% target. magic_link_requested=0 for 14+ days confirms removal held; gains are real (+12pp from 33%) but short of target.","confidence":"med","tags":["funnel","signup","measurement","predictions"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-04-remove-magic-link"}
{"type": "prediction", "id": "PRED-2026-06-18-try-generate-gap", "date": "2026-06-18", "action": "Fix the /try garment\u2192generate 46% drop: make the Generate button unmissable after a garment is added (more prominent CTA, load-state feedback, or inline 'Now generate your try-on' prompt on the garment-added screen)", "linked": "CC-rank-4", "metric": "home_signup_pct", "baseline": 10.1, "predicted": 12.5, "horizon_days": 14, "due": "2026-07-02", "rationale": "510 /try viewers \u2192 199 category selected \u2192 169 garment added \u2192 only 91 clicked Generate (46% drop, 78 high-intent garment-adders lost). Recovering 30% of those 78 at current downstream generate\u2192signup rate (57.6%, 53/92) adds ~13 signers, lifting /try view\u2192signup from 10.1% to ~12.5%. Wave 3 paid traffic starts today, growing the denominator fast and making this testable within 14d. Calibration thin: single day this alarm appeared. Moot if no UI fix shipped by Jul 2.", "scoring": "resolve on post-fix /try tbs cohort view\u2192signup rate vs 10.1% baseline; NOT blended home_signup_pct (which tracks homepage, not /try); require >=7d post-fix tbs* data; Wave 3 confound: if paid quality drops, rate may fall even with the fix; score vs cohort not time-series. Moot if fix not shipped by Jul 2.", "status": "resolved", "actual": 10.9, "verdict": "moot", "resolved_date": "2026-07-08", "lesson_id": "LES-2026-07-08-try-generate-moot", "resolution_note": "moot: fix never shipped (per Experiments coverage read); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-18-qa-generate-gap-distinct","date":"2026-06-18","lesson":"The /try funnel has two separate leaks that require distinct fixes: (1) category-selection drop (39% pass-through, affects all /try visitors) and (2) garment→generate drop (54% pass-through among higher-intent garment-adders, 46% loss at highest intent). QA today refuted a draft that merged both into the category fix: different steps, different user states, different root causes. Rank them separately.","evidence":"QA Jun 18: data.js funnelSuggestions surfaces garment→generate drop (91/169=53.8%) as a new distinct alarm; CC rank-7 category fix (199/510=39%) predates it; PRED-2026-06-09-tbs-category-fix covers the category step only. Added CC rank-4 for the generate drop.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","try","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-18-try-generate-gap"}
{"type": "prediction", "id": "PRED-2026-06-19-onboarding-model-filter", "date": "2026-06-19", "action": "Pre-filter the onboarding model gallery to ~5-8 matches based on the user's Q1 segment answer (kids/swim/womenswear), eliminating the cold browse of 50+ models", "linked": "CC-rank-3", "metric": "activation_rate", "baseline": 51, "predicted": 57, "horizon_days": 14, "due": "2026-07-03", "rationale": "63 of 77 recent signups (14d since Jun 4) answered all 3 onboarding questions but only 29 picked a model (38% pass-through, 54% drop at model selection). After model pick, 28/29 generated (97%), so model selection is almost the entire loss, not generation. The questionnaire already knows the segment; surfacing 5-8 matching models instead of 50+ cold eliminates choice paralysis at the pinch point. Recovering 30% of the 34 who bailed at model pick in the cohort would recover ~10 activations. Conservative 6pp call on thin sample (14d, n=77). All-time spine (82/162=51%) is the more stable baseline. Moot if not shipped by Jul 3.", "scoring": "resolve on onboarding Q3-to-model-pick pass-through rate post-fix vs 29/63=46% baseline; activation_rate (spine) is directional; require >=14d post-fix data; moot if fix not shipped by Jul 3", "status": "resolved", "actual": 46, "verdict": "moot", "resolved_date": "2026-07-08", "lesson_id": "LES-2026-07-08-onboarding-moot", "resolution_note": "moot: fix never shipped (per Experiments coverage read); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-19-qa-c4-stale-status","date":"2026-06-19","lesson":"The commandCenter C4 status ('12 recipients, 0% open') was stale at write time: live.lifecycle in the same data.js showed C4 at 20 recipients, 20.0% open, 0 clicks. Deliverability was fine; the problem is CTA copy, not spam. A stale CC status inverted the diagnostic (spam vs copy), causing a wrong investigation brief. Verify lifecycle stats directly from live.lifecycle on each reasoning pass, not from a prior CC status.","evidence":"QA Jun 19: data.js live.lifecycle C4=20 recipients/20% open vs CC rank-6 status citing 12/0%. CC was written before the Klaviyo pull refreshed. The 0% open alarm was incorrect; investigation priority and direction changed on QA.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","lifecycle","email","process"],"source_pred":null}
{"type": "prediction", "id": "PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework", "date": "2026-06-22", "action": "Rework Convert C2-C5 + AHA B1/B2 paid-ask CTAs to one concrete action line plus a direct /studio-or-checkout link; current CTAs draw 0 clicks across 105 (Convert) + 24 (AHA) recipients despite 20-42% opens.", "linked": "CC-rank-2", "metric": "email_click", "baseline": 0.0, "predicted": 5.0, "horizon_days": 14, "due": "2026-07-06", "rationale": "Aggregate email_click has been 0.0 for 5+ straight days while email_open holds 31-33% -- a pure CTA failure, not deliverability or timing. One concrete action + a direct link should produce nonzero clicks. Conservative target (5%) given thin calibration (0.33, n=3). Contingent on the live-flow edit shipping (escalate-gated); moot if unshipped by due date.", "status": "resolved", "actual": 0.0, "verdict": "moot", "resolved_date": "2026-07-08", "lesson_id": "LES-2026-07-08-cta-rework-moot", "resolution_note": "moot: fix never shipped (per Experiments coverage read); excluded from calibration"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-try-data-location","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The tbs /try funnel numbers (category pass-through, garment->generate drop) live in live.meta.funnelSuggestions and the experiments/learning prose, NOT in live.funnel.stages -- so the Funnel read-agent (which reads only live.funnel) will miss them and a date-stamp of 'not in today's data.js' is wrong. Before stamping any /try metric as absent or stale, grep the WHOLE data.js including funnelSuggestions.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 22: funnelSuggestions[0].evidence = '622 viewed -> 230 category -> 198 garment -> 105 Generate' dated Jun 22 'unchanged from last cycle'; I had labeled ranks 7 & 9 'last measured Jun 19, not in data.js' -- wrong, corrected.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","data-source"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-log-clean-baseline","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"A clean, observable-now baseline (e.g. email_click=0 across 129 recipients) should be logged as a prediction at decision/queue time, not deferred to ship-time -- 'log the PRED when it ships' risks losing the pre-state and lets the top fix-lever run unbet. Logging a bet does not require shipping the fix; mark it moot-if-unshipped.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jun 22: the new #2 lever (Convert C2-C5 rework) had a crisp 0-click baseline but no PRED; the roadmap deferred it. Logged PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework in response.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","ledger","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-22-cta-rework"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-qa-checkout-window","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The checkout-starter count differs by view/window: same-user spine = 10, reach (all) = 11, d30 reach = 5. Always cite which view a checkout figure comes from. A skeptic refuted '10' as '7', but 7 was an OLD status's d30 figure, not the live spine -- the live spine count (10) stands. Reconcile to live.funnel.spine, and never let a stale CC status's number override the live spine.","evidence":"data.js live.funnel.spine 'Started checkout' count=10; stages.checkout.counts {d7:1,d30:5,all:11}; the disputed '7' matched no live value (it was a prior status's d30 reach).","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-22-meta-feed-rootcause","date":"2026-06-22","lesson":"The Meta feed 'froze' at $241.52 not because the feed broke but because the autopilot's lifetime pull was hardcoded to ONE campaign (CAMPAIGN_ID, the Jun-2 relaunch) while Ablo spend had spread across 3 campaigns (paused May-20 original $512/25, Jun-3 LP-test $460/52 ACTIVE, relaunch $241/29). Real lifetime is $1,332/111/$12.01 CPL. Fixed in autopilot lib/meta.py + run_cycle.py: lifetime report now paginates all campaigns, name-matches 'Ablo' (excludes 200+ unrelated 'AI .' junk campaigns in the shared ad account), sums via date_preset=maximum; the campaign the autopilot ACTS on is unchanged. Heuristic: when a campaign-scoped metric looks frozen, first check whether spend moved to a sibling campaign the scope misses, before assuming a broken feed or dark ads. This is the true root cause behind LES-2026-06-15-meta-dark.","evidence":"meta.lifetime_insights_ablo() live: 9 adsets $1332.89/111 regs; account-level 30d showed 3 Ablo campaigns + ~$140 AI-junk; dry-run regenerated LATEST.md to $1332.89/111/$12.01.","confidence":"high","tags":["campaigns","data-integrity","autopilot"],"source_pred":""}

{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-activate-miss","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"The Activate email flow did not lift activation: activation_rate fell 69->50 over the 21-day horizon despite the flow being live since May 19. Email cannot fix a product paralysis step. The real collapse is at onboarding model-pick (79% finish the 3 questions, only 33% pick a model), compounded by paid mix-shift (paid 44% vs direct 66%). Activation needs the model-gallery pre-filter (product), not more email.","evidence":"history.jsonl activation_rate 2026-06-24=50; live.funnel.onboarding 79% Q3 -> 33% pick -> 32% generate; activationBefore 69/after 38.","confidence":"high","tags":["lifecycle","funnel","activation"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-03-activate-flow"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-tbs-category-miss","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"MOOT, not scored: the /try category-selection fix never shipped (home_signup_pct 10.4 vs 10.5 baseline, no step-change), so the bet got no fair test and is excluded from calibration. The leak persists. Per the prediction's own 'moot if unshipped' clause, resolve unshipped bets as moot, never as a hypothesis miss.","evidence":"history.jsonl home_signup_pct 2026-06-24=10.4 (baseline 10.5); Funnel agent: no ship evidence, climb is org drift.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-09-tbs-category-fix"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-checkout-outreach-miss","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"MOOT, not scored: the Alejo-gated 1:1 outreach to the 10 checkout-starters was not executed before the Jun-20 window, so payment_rate (drifted 6->5) cannot be attributed to it. Excluded from calibration per the moot-if-unexecuted clause. The first sale stays gated on execution, not analysis.","evidence":"history.jsonl payment_rate 2026-06-24=5; paying_customers=0 all window; outreach unconfirmed/undone.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","paid","process"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-17-checkout-outreach"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-escalate-gated-calibration","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"Resolve 'moot if unshipped' predictions as MOOT (excluded from calibration), not miss: folding non-execution into the hit-rate makes the number measure org throughput, not judgment, and biases the OS toward false timidity. Corrected this run (tbs-category + checkout-outreach re-resolved moot; only activate-flow, which shipped and declined, scored a true miss). Going forward, tag a prediction's execution owner; if the action is outside Claude's control, prefer not logging a calibration-scored bet at all.","evidence":"3 due predictions all missed 2026-06-24; tbs-category + checkout-outreach missed purely because the action never shipped/happened.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","process","calibration"],"source_pred":""}

{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-qa-moot-clause","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"A prediction carrying a 'moot if unshipped/unexecuted' clause MUST resolve as moot (verdict:moot, excluded from calibration) when the action provably did not happen, not as a miss. build.py only counts hit/partial/miss toward n, so moot is the correct, honest exclusion. Scoring non-execution as a miss distorted today's calibration to 0.17 before correction.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jun 24; build.py:1568 _VERDICT_PTS excludes moot from n.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","process","calibration"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-qa-escalate-stuck-lever","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"When the top actionable lever (Convert C2-C5 CTA rework) sits escalate-gated and UNSHIPPED across multiple consecutive cycles, escalate the execution blocker as the run's HEADLINE signal to Alejo, not a status line. 'Discipline over a forced launch' is correct only while the gated work is actually moving; here it is not, and the first customer is gated on it.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jun 24; Convert rework drafted Jun 22, still unshipped Jun 24; 121 recipients, 0 clicks, windows elapsed.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","process","execution"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-qa-onboarding-verbatim","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"Copy onboarding sub-funnel percentages verbatim from live.funnel.onboarding.steps each run: a draft cited Q3 79% (file 80%) and generate 32% (file 35%), a retype drift. Grep the exact step counts before asserting them.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 24: onboarding steps Q3 48/60=80%, picked 20/60=33%, generated 21/60=35%.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-24-qa-unpersisted-ctr","date":"2026-06-24","lesson":"Do not cite live-read Meta ad-set CTRs (e.g. Swim 3.96%, Men 2.04%) as fact: they are unpersisted and contradicted the only persisted CTRs (campaignsCurated.bestDay swim 2.97%, men 1.91%). Use persisted figures or state qualitatively (Swim best, Men weakest) until the segment read is written to data.js/history.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 24: 3.96/2.04 absent from all files; persisted bestDay swim 2.97% / men 1.91%.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","campaigns","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-29-post-aha-email-miss","date":"2026-06-29","lesson":"Wiring a post-AHA Klaviyo email did NOT lift paid conversion: payment_rate fell 8->5 and checkout-start rate among aha-reachers dropped 18%->13% (10/79). The AHA flow logged ~0 CTA clicks across recipients, so the email mechanism never fired. The bottleneck is the in-product money-ask and the missing real purchase path, not email coverage.","evidence":"history payment_rate 8(Jun5)->5(Jun26-29); AHA B1/B2 0 clicks; 10 checkout-starters all-time, 0 purchase_completed.","confidence":"high","tags":["lifecycle","paid","funnel"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-05-post-aha-email"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-29-rageclicks-miss","date":"2026-06-29","lesson":"Escalating the /studio rage-click cluster did NOT lift activation: activation_rate drifted 53->48-49, the wrong direction. Activation is dominated by paid-vs-organic mix (organic ~57% vs paid ~41% same-user), not the rage-click UX fix. Predict activation per-source, not on the blended rate.","evidence":"history activation_rate 53(Jun12)->49(Jun26)->48(Jun29); spine organic model 57% vs paid 41%; no studio control fix shipped.","confidence":"high","tags":["funnel","activation","paid"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-12-studio-rageclicks"}
{"type":"prediction","id":"PRED-2026-06-29-paid-wedge-gap","date":"2026-06-29","action":"Queue the paid value-first landing test (Kids/Swim paid -> wedge-led landing, measure paid aha->pricing) and escalate the in-product aha price-ask. Structural bet: paid volume without the wedge landing, and email-only money-asks, cannot lift payment_rate.","linked":"CC-rank-2","metric":"payment_rate","baseline":5,"predicted":5,"horizon_days":14,"due":"2026-07-13","rationale":"Paid is 57% of signups (112/196) but converts to checkout at 1% (1/112) vs organic 11% (9/84); email money-ask CTAs log ~0-1% clicks; 0 purchase_completed all-time. Neither resuming paid volume nor reworking email CTAs can move payment_rate. Only an in-product price-ask at the aha (CC#3, product-owned) can. Absent that, payment_rate holds 5.","scoring":"hit iff payment_rate stays <=5 at due (money step is the wall); 6 = partial/ambiguous; >6 = miss (inspect what moved it). Null/negative prediction: hit band == baseline, no cushion.","status":"open"}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-29-qa-activation-58","date":"2026-06-29","lesson":"Do not transcribe 58% as organic activation: organic same-user model-generated rate is 57% (paid 41%). The 58 is the signup-modal loss figure. Grep live.funnel.spine.steps[].organic.pct before asserting per-source activation.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 29: spine organic model 57%, not 58.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-29-qa-convert-ctr","date":"2026-06-29","lesson":"Use the persisted lifecycle agg click rate (Convert 1.2%), not a subagent's rounded recall (0.6%). Cite from live.lifecycle agg, not agent prose.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jun 29: Convert agg click 1.2%, open 30.9%.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","lifecycle","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-06-29-qa-null-pred-band","date":"2026-06-29","lesson":"When logging a null/no-move prediction, set the hit band equal to the baseline (==5), not baseline+1. A 1-point cushion on a noisy n=6 metric makes 'no move' unfalsifiable and inflates apparent hits.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jun 29: PRED-2026-06-29-paid-wedge-gap hit band <=6 was looser than baseline 5; tightened.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","calibration"],"source_pred":"PRED-2026-06-29-paid-wedge-gap"}

