{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-01-qa-spine-denominators","date":"2026-07-01","lesson":"Re-derive every paid-vs-organic ratio from live.funnel.spine.denominators each run: CC #2 carried the prior cycle's 196/112/84 while live was 202/116/86 (paid 1/116 not 1/112, organic 9/86 not 9/84). The percentage was unchanged, which masked the stale raw counts. Never carry forward last cycle's denominators.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jul 1; live spine denominators all=202/paid=116/organic=86.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-01-qa-organic-activation-drift","date":"2026-07-01","lesson":"Organic model-activation is 56% in the file, mis-stated 57% again (same 56-vs-57/58 drift flagged Jun 29). Grep spine.steps['Generated a model'].organic.pct verbatim; treat 57/58 as a known miscopy trigger for this metric.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jul 1; spine organic model pct=56.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","funnel","numbers"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-01-qa-unpersisted-adset-3x","date":"2026-07-01","lesson":"THIRD repeat (Jun 11, Jun 24, Jul 1): unpersisted live-read ad-set CPL/CTR (e.g. Swim $4.61, Kids $35) were written into the Command Center as sourced facts. A 'not persisted' caveat is not enough, the precise numbers still read as sourced. Rule: state segment performance qualitatively (Swim best/cheapest, Kids hot) OR persist the ad-set read to data.js/history first, then cite. Recurrence means this needs a build-time guard, not another lesson, promote in the monthly audit.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jul 1; '4.61' absent from data.js; persisted bestDay is the only sourced segment CTR.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","campaigns","numbers","promote-to-skill"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-01-qa-stage-the-artifact","date":"2026-07-01","lesson":"When a run's headline is 'execution not diagnosis' for the Nth consecutive cycle, the reversible OS-ownable move is to PRODUCE the staged artifact (drafted CTA copy / at-aha price-ask spec as a ready-to-paste diff), not to re-escalate verbally. 'Drafted, waiting' with run writes:[] means nothing was actually staged. Acted on this run: wrote state/drafts/cta-rework-2026-07-01.md so shipping is a paste. Each future 'execution-blocked' cycle must ship the reversible half.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jul 1; refresh-log Jun15/22/24/29 all end 'ship the CTA rework (drafted)' with no staged copy until now.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","execution","process","promote-to-skill"],"source_pred":""}

{"type": "lesson", "id": "LES-2026-07-08-first-customer", "date": "2026-07-08", "lesson": "FIRST PAYING CUSTOMER (Jul 2): an ORGANIC/direct user on the Growth ANNUAL plan, converted IN-APP a day after the aha via the pricing prompt shown at try-on, NOT via email or paid. Path: signup -> onboarding -> import product -> try-on (aha, pricing prompt shown) -> left -> returned 19h later -> checkout -> buy (mobile). Implication: the product converts high-intent organic users at the aha moment; the real conversion path is the in-app aha-pricing-prompt + a return visit. Email (click=0) and paid (checkouts concentrate in Direct, not Meta) did NOT produce it. The queued email/product fixes were NOT the lever for customer #1.", "evidence": "PostHog distinct_id RvJ1rzpRqI_1, plan_tier=growth billing_interval=year, all touchpoints $direct; email_click 0 all window; PostHog checkouts Direct 11 vs Meta 2.", "confidence": "high", "tags": ["funnel", "paid", "milestone", "lifecycle"], "source_pred": ""}
