{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-08-qa-report-tested-rate","date":"2026-07-08","lesson":"When the moot pile is large (now 6 of 12 resolved), report the TESTED-bet rate (1 hit / 6 scored) alongside calibration 0.17, not the excluded-n number alone. 0.17 is low-information when half the bets never got a fair test; the real signal is 'stop logging bets the OS cannot execute' (applied this run: no new prediction).","evidence":"QA both skeptics Jul 8; 6 moot / 5 miss / 1 hit; all 6 moot are unshipped/unexecuted.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","predictions","calibration"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-08-qa-moot-count-derive","date":"2026-07-08","lesson":"Derive the moot count arithmetically as resolved(counts.resolved) minus scored(calibration.n) from the SAME rebuilt data.js, and never report it from a pre-rebuild snapshot. A skeptic read a stale data.js (resolved 9, moot 3) before the rebuild while the ledger already had 6 moot. Rebuild before quoting ledger counts.","evidence":"QA numbers skeptic Jul 8 saw resolved=9 (pre-rebuild) vs file 12 resolved / 6 moot.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","predictions","process"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-08-qa-unpersisted-adset-4x","date":"2026-07-08","lesson":"FOURTH repeat: a budget-reallocation recommendation (Swim vs Kids) was anchored on unpersisted live-read ad-set CPLs. A 'not persisted' label is honest but the fix is to state segment direction QUALITATIVELY for any money call, or persist the ad-set read to data.js/history first. This recurs enough to need a build-time guard (reject numeric ad-set CPL/CTR in commandCenter unless it grep-matches a persisted key). Promote to SKILL in the monthly audit.","evidence":"QA both skeptics Jul 8; $7.27/$34.73 absent from data.js/history.","confidence":"high","tags":["qa","campaigns","numbers","promote-to-skill"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-08-qa-milestone-n1","date":"2026-07-08","lesson":"Milestone framing must not over-read n=1: 'the product converts organic users at the aha' as a general capability over-reaches one annual buyer. The defensible framing ties the single conversion to the weeks of channel data it is consistent with (email 0 clicks, Direct 11 vs Meta 2, organic 10% vs paid 2% to pricing). The re-rank is grounded in the channel data, not the lone payer.","evidence":"QA calls skeptic Jul 8; LES-2026-06-12-channel-quality-gap.","confidence":"med","tags":["qa","funnel","milestone"],"source_pred":""}
{"type":"lesson","id":"LES-2026-07-08-attribution-artifact","date":"2026-07-08","lesson":"The 'organic converts ~11x better than paid' conclusion was an ATTRIBUTION ARTIFACT, not a real channel signal. Evidence-based first-touch reclassification of 224 signups: paid 64% (mostly UTM-tracked), true organic 14%, and 22% UNATTRIBUTED (UTM stripped in mobile in-app browsers + the ablo.ai->studio.ablo.ai cross-domain hop). PostHog files that 22% under 'organic/direct', which inflated organic. The first paying customer is in the unattributed bucket (landed direct on the app root), NOT organic. Built an evidence-based attribution layer into build.py (classify_true_source + fetch_true_attribution) that classifies by referrer+landing, excludes the email auth loop (18 fake 'signups'), and reports an integrity % (only 76% reliably attributed). Real product fix (UTM pass-through + CAPI) stays flagged. Rule: never read PostHog's paid-vs-organic split literally when UTMs are lossy, reclassify from first-touch evidence and report what you cannot see.","evidence":"build.py fetch_true_attribution live: paid 132/organic 28/lost 46 of 206 acq; payer first-touch $direct on studio.ablo.ai/; ChatGPT 5 signups; auth loop 18 excluded.","confidence":"high","tags":["measurement","campaigns","attribution","qa"],"source_pred":""}
